===========
Compilation
===========

This project can be compiled using the provided Makefile.
A C++ compiler supporting c++11 is needed.

Just run the following command inside the project folder:

$ make

=========
Operation
=========

After compilation, the assembler is located at ./build/bin/asxe.

> ./build/bin/asxe
Assemble SIC/XE assembly code into object code.
Usage: asxe <file> [<file> ...]

> ./build/bin/asxe ./tests/P2sample.sic
Read 584 bytes from ./tests/P2sample.sic
Pass 1 complete for ./tests/P2sample.sic
Pass 2 complete for ./tests/P2sample.sic
Wrote object code: ./tests/P2sample.l
Wrote symbol table: ./tests/P2sample.st

=====
Notes
=====

This project uses the c++11 standard library instead of calling libc or any
system calls directly.

Line breaks are done by printing "\n" instead of using "std::endl" to
avoid unnecessary flushes of the output buffer.

No C-style casts.

================
Missing Features
================
- No macro support
- No support for multiple program blocks (USE directive)